<Layout title="About Econified | Work and Pay Calculators" description="What Econified does, how its examples are built, and where its calculations stop." noAds={true}>
<main class="container" style="max-width:780px;"><article class="glass-panel">
<h1>About Econified</h1>
<h2>Who operates Econified?</h2>
<p>Econified is operated by Ausland Teknologi, a sole proprietorship. For questions, feedback or corrections, contact <a href="mailto:info@econified.com">info@econified.com</a>.</p>
<p>Econified is an independent project for comparing the numbers behind work decisions: a commute, a contract rate, a promotion or two job offers. The calculators let you change assumptions and see how those assumptions affect the result.</p>
<h2>What the tools provide</h2><p>Each tool describes its formula and limits. Worked examples are illustrative scenarios, not salary surveys or predictions. US concepts such as W-2 employment, 1099 contracting and 401(k) benefits are identified where relevant.</p>
<h2>How to check a result</h2><p>Start with your payslip, offer documents, actual spending and expected schedule. Read the formula below the calculator. Separate cash from benefits and the personal value of time. Official sources support the rules described; they do not endorse Econified or certify its results.</p>
<p>See <a href="/how-it-works/">methodology and corrections</a> for calculation scope and the changes made during the September 2026 quality review.</p>
<h2>Data and privacy</h2><p>Calculations run in your browser. An optional account can store decision cases you explicitly save. Currency display uses a third-party exchange-rate service. Read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for storage and third-party services.</p>
<h2>Feedback</h2><p>If a result appears wrong, <a href="/contact/">report the calculator, an anonymized example and the expected result</a>. Please omit personal financial documents.</p>
</article></main></Layout>
